# NET-1 pass 5: the server's GameMode names the pawn (UE DefaultPawnClass): DesertServer --pawn <assets:X.deprefab>,
# its AssetHandle (FromKey of the stable key) travels in the Welcome (protocol 3); the client spawns that prefab for
# every remote pawn and, when the open level names no pawn (WP_Protocol), for its own pawn too, and possesses it.
# A refused Hello is logged on the server with the reason and both sides' protocol/cook/token fields (UE PreLogin
# ErrorMessage) and sent to the client. Pass 4's "token invalid" was a STALE DesertServer from an earlier run still
# bound to 27031 with another secret (the new one failed "cannot listen"); the runner now waits for "listening" and
# execs the server so its kill reaches it.
# Runner: <scratch>/NET-1/run_net1e.sh B|A, logs <scratch>/NET-1/logs/net1e-<B|A>; client scene WP_Protocol, shot
