# Тогда [net1_two_clients] clientB_view.png: B's own pawn at (0,92,650) and A's pawn at x ~ +1000, z -500 (displaced
#   2000 cm from its spawn at x -1000); editorB.log "spawned the server's pawn prefab" + "remote pawn ... spawned";
#   server.log "admitted: 2  refused: 0".
# Тогда [net1_two_clients_A] clientA_view.png: A's own pawn at x ~ +1000 (editorA.log "walked 2000 cm"), B's pawn at
#   (0,92,650).
# NET-1 pass 4: the EDITOR plays as a network client (UE PIE "Play As Client"): Editor --play --connect ip:port
# --net-token HEX --net-cooked <cooked world> - Engine/Net/ClientNetDriver possesses the server's pawn for this
# connection (NetRoleComponent Autonomous), spawns the Default Pawn prefab for every other player (Simulated,
# Scene::AddRemotePlayer) and writes both from the replicated state each frame; PhysicsECSSystem does not move a pawn
# with a net role; input = the own pawn's MoveInput on the 60 Hz net step (or --net-walk-cm for a headless run).
# Runner: <scratch>/NET-1/run_net1d.sh B|A (one GPU editor per machine: B's view and A's view are two runs), logs
# <scratch>/NET-1/logs/net1d-<B|A>. Client scene Starter (WP_Protocol names no Default Pawn / PlayerStart).
# Тогда [net1d_B_view] clientB_view.png: B's camera behind its own pawn at its spawn (0,92,650); A's pawn ~11.5 m ahead,
#   moved 2000 cm along +X (editorB.log "[Net] remote pawn ... spawned" then pawns line with A at x ~ +1000);
#   server.log union lists server + player 1 + player 2.
# Тогда [net1d_A_view] clientA_view.png: A's own pawn walked 2000 cm along +X (editorA.log "walked 2000 cm"),
#   B's pawn replicated at (0,92,650).
# NET-1 pass 3: two clients see each other - N players in the Scene (Scene::GetPlayers, [0] = local), the mesh of
# one in DesertServer (Desert/Net MeshOfOne: Gateway + PawnSimulation + InProcessReplicationStore behind
# IGatewayLink / ISimLink / IReplicationStore), a pawn spawned per admitted connection (Spawn on the Rpc lane),
# 30 Hz transform snapshots on the State lane with the per-connection input ack, client interpolation 100 ms behind
# the server clock; input -> server only (numbered steps, last 3 per message, client InputRing dropped to the ack -
# NET-4 replays from it). The clients of this pass are headless players (DesertNetProbe --bot, the same
# ReplicationClient the engine's net driver will run); the editor windows are the next pass (REMAINDER).
